        <argsstring>() const noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>operator-</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::type_traits::integral_constant::operator-</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Unary minus operator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The result has the type of <computeroutput>N</computeroutput>, not the type promoted by the built-in unary minus, so <computeroutput>-1<ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1ga265f8609ef3d6ead78c7a66825553e24" kindref="member">_i8</ref></computeroutput> is an <computeroutput>int8_t</computeroutput>. The negation of an unsigned value wraps around, as for <computeroutput>unsigned int</computeroutput> in C++ (<computeroutput>-1<ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1gaf27e37e2e29af1a3ffd5c4fb07e77ff9" kindref="member">_u8</ref></computeroutput> is 255). The negation of the minimum of a signed type does not fit in the type, so it is a compilation error.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>An <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1integral__constant" kindref="compound">integral_constant</ref></computeroutput> with value <computeroutput>-N</computeroutput>, converted to the type of <computeroutput>N</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
The built-in unary minus promotes the types narrower than <computeroutput>int</computeroutput>, so its result is converted back to the type of <computeroutput>N</computeroutput>. For the unsigned types, the value is subtracted from zero, which, after the conversion, gives the value modulo 2^n for all widths. For the signed types, the minimum is rejected before the negation, which would otherwise overflow for <computeroutput>int</computeroutput> and the wider types. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/micro-test-plus-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus/values.h" line="261" column="7" bodyfile="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/micro-test-plus-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus/inlines/values-inlines.h" bodystart="128" bodyend="148"/>
      </memberdef>
