    <briefdescription>
<para>Struct template representing a generic integral constant. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>N</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The compile-time constant value.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1integral__constant" kindref="compound">integral_constant</ref></computeroutput> struct template provides a compile-time constant value of an integral type, created by the integer literals. It inherits from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value__base_1ad2d04a9ef0d53c48107b13005ec0877d" kindref="member">value_base</ref>&lt;decltype(N)&gt;</computeroutput>, which supplies the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value__base_1abb9873b49614cc55fae3f6dda7b08b48" kindref="member">value_type</ref></computeroutput> alias, the runtime value storage, the explicit conversion operator, and the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value__base_1a9199f28db3a365b60ca6ef17053cec2a" kindref="member">get()</ref></computeroutput> accessor.</para>
<para>This struct retains the compile-time <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1value" kindref="compound">value</ref></computeroutput> constant and provides a unary minus operator to obtain the negative value as a new <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1integral__constant" kindref="compound">integral_constant</ref></computeroutput> instance, of the same type. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
